{"name":"Blindfold","hex":"#4a4f51","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blindfold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering, usually a bandage, for the eyes, blocking light to the eyes.","Anything that obscures the vision."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the eyes covered so as to obscure vision","Thoughtless; reckless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blindfold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blindfold","blocks":[{"text":"A blindfold is a garment, usually of cloth, tied to one's head to cover the eyes to disable the wearer's sight. While a properly fitted blindfold prevents sight even if the eyes are open, a poorly tied or trick blindfold may let the wearer see around or even through the blindfold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Truly_and_Bluford_Asleep_on_Middeck_-_GPN-2000-001079.jpg/330px-Truly_and_Bluford_Asleep_on_Middeck_-_GPN-2000-001079.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blindfold"},{"title":"Blindfold (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Blindfold is a fictional character, a mutant appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character is usually depicted as a member of the student body of the Xavier Institute in X-Men-related comic books. She first appeared in Astonishing X-Men, vol. 3 #7 and was created by Joss Whedon and John Cassaday."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Blindfold_%28comics%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blindfold_(character)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Sleep_mask.jpg/250px-Sleep_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Sleep_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th